# Files kept in the repo but never sent to visitors.
#
# Named explicitly rather than by wildcard. An earlier "images/*.JPG" here was
# matched case-insensitively and silently excluded all seventeen lowercase
# .jpg diagrams, so every reconstruction page rendered a broken image on the
# deployed site while working perfectly in local preview.
#
# The page requests 42 files from images/: the 24 .webp and 18 .jpg
# listed nowhere below (share-card.jpg among them - it is the social
# preview image, fetched by Facebook and iMessage, so it must deploy). Everything below is source material or a working
# master that nothing on the page links to.

# The repository itself. Cloudflare uploads the asset directory as-is, and
# the directory is the project root, so .git was being shipped as part of
# the website. On 2026-10-10 its pack file passed 25 MiB and every deploy
# began failing with "Asset too large". It had been uploading all along.
.git
.git/*
.gitignore

build-trail.py
wip/*
wrangler.jsonc
.assetsignore
.DS_Store
.claude/*

